      "crowdScaled": true,
      "why": "The murmur of the crowd standing IN the courts, as distinct from voices carrying up from the city. The project now instances thousands of figures plus 24 speaking residents, and a court full of people that makes no sound is the loudest wrong note there is. Continuous, but the take and its pitch are re-drawn every pass, and at run time the level follows the live head count through MikdashSoundscape::CrowdMurmurGain -- so an empty court at dawn is silent, not quiet. The church take is the primary because its reverberation is masonry rather than a room; the festival take is the busier alternative."
